<section class="solaris-section solaris-assumptions" id="assumptions">
  <div class="solaris-container solaris-container-narrow">
    <details class="solaris-details">
      <summary>Simulation assumptions</summary>
      <ul class="solaris-assumptions-list">
        <li>Simplified clear-sky irradiance model</li>
        <li>Simplified solar-position model</li>
        <li>Idealized panel response</li>
        <li>No cloud dynamics</li>
        <li>No shading</li>
        <li>No temperature losses</li>
        <li>No inverter losses</li>
        <li>No mechanical losses</li>
        <li>Simplified tracking controller</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="solaris-scientific-note">
        SOLARIS is a physics-inspired interactive solar tracking simulator. Simulated energy gains
        illustrate the underlying geometry and optimization behavior — they do not represent
        real-world measured performance of a physical solar installation.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
